<p>I am too tired to read this properly and will give a more coherent response to the piece in the morning when I have fully consumed it, but I expect that this will not be much different from my initial reaction, which is</p>
<p><span style="font-size:xx-large;">oh god oh fuck</span></p>
<p>Edit: Okay, read it.</p>
<p>So THAT'S why RBG can't die! sorry. In all seriousness, this had some truly wonderful moments - Tiffany Trump's entire scene was hysterical, the &quot;Alto Clef NOPE&quot; make me chuckle, the repeated attempts by the centrist to try and get other people to see this is as a good thing, and him being shot down immediately.</p>
<p>This was an enjoyable experience all around for me. It's stupid, but it brought me joy. The best thing about this though, is that you avoided the easy + alluring trap of implying/saying that the involvement of the Foundation and the anomalous in general was why Trump got elected. That would be pretty tasteless + inconsiderate of the real social problems that led to it.</p>
<p>Overall, easy +1</p>

